      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 503: 🟡 `ADD_REACTION` validation says the target must be a visible message, but the check only verifies `targetMessageIndex \u003e\u003d 0`. This allows generating reaction commits for messages already deleted (empty `body`/`tid`), which then become no-op history noise and can reduce DST signal quality. Reuse the same visibility predicate later used in `computeExpectedMessages` (non-empty `CommitKey::BODY` or `CommitKey::TID`) and reject the event when the target is deleted.",
      "revId": "923bb6009221d05b5f60a4414a3b354ea2b45c9f",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
